\end{aligned}
\end{align*}

## Step 10: Simplify 

We know that $\cos(12) = -\cos 0$. We also have that $\cos(12) = \cos(12 - 2 \pi) = \cos(-12)$.

To make the final calculations easier, let's only use the identity $\cos(-x) = \cos x$. 

